      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**The Being** (1983) represents peak low-budget 1980s creature feature schlock, following in the radioactive footsteps of films like **Prophecy** (1979) and <a href=\"/movie/29343\" class=\"movie-title\">Humanoids from the Deep</a> (1980). Shot in Idaho with a meager budget, it stars Martin Landau in one of his many paycheck roles during his career slump before **Ed Wood** (1994) revitalized his trajectory. The film's mutant monster, created through practical effects that vary wildly in quality, emerges from toxic waste - playing directly into 1980s environmental horror trends seen in <a href=\"/movie/23730\" class=\"movie-title\">C.H.U.D.</a> (1984) and <a href=\"/movie/44932\" class=\"movie-title\">Without Warning</a> (1980)."
      },
